le":"font-size: 16px; font-weight: 900; color: rgb(134, 239, 172); margin-bottom: 4px;"},"✓ SAFE — passes both yield and buckling checks"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 12px; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #cbd5e1); margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.55;"},"Two different checks, both passed: the material is strong enough (yield), and no piece is so long and thin that it would snap sideways (buckling)."],["DIV",{"style":"display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #e2e8f0);"},["STRONG",{"style":"color: rgb(134, 239, 172); min-width: 150px;"},"✓ Strength (yield)"],["SPAN",{},"Safety factor 36.30 (max stress 10 MPa vs nominal strength 350 MPa)"]],["DIV",{"style":"display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #e2e8f0);"},["STRONG",{"style":"color: rgb(134, 239, 172); min-width: 150px;"},"✓ Stability (buckling)"],["SPAN",{},"Governing member DL0: P_cr 716 kN vs compression 134 kN; length 6.7 m; slenderness 196 (pinned ends K=1; solid square section)"]],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #cbd5e1); line-height: 1.6;"},"Both checks meet this lab’s target for the current applied load. A safety factor of 2 is a learning target, not a bridge code approval."]],["DIV",{"style":"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 12px;"},["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Max chord force"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(248, 113, 113); margin-top: 2px;"},"135 kN"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The biggest pull or squeeze in the long top/bottom pieces. (1 kN is about the weight of a washing machine.)"]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Max diagonal force"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(96, 165, 250); margin-top: 2px;"},"134 kN"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The biggest force in the zig-zag pieces. Diagonals work hardest near the supports."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Max stress"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(245, 158, 11); margin-top: 2px;"},"10 MPa"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"Force squeezed into each bit of material. Must stay well BELOW the yield number beside it."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Material yield"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"350 MPa"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The stress where this material starts to permanently bend or tear. Your ceiling."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Buckling load (P_cr)"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(167, 139, 250); margin-top: 2px;"},"716 kN"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The push at which the weakest strut snaps sideways, like a spaghetti noodle pressed from both ends."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Weakest strut"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(167, 139, 250); margin-top: 2px;"},"DL0"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The piece closest to buckling. Find it in the picture above; the whole bridge is only as safe as this one piece."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Slenderness ratio (L/r)"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(167, 139, 250); margin-top: 2px;"},"196"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"Length divided by thickness. Long and thin = wobbly. Real design codes stop at about 200."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Push-back at each support"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"75 kN"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"How hard each end pushes back up. The two ends together carry the whole load."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Diagonal angle"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"63°"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"Changing the angle changes both the member length and force. Compare designs under the same load to see the trade-off."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Total member length"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"146.5 m"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"All the pieces laid end to end. More length = more material = more cost."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Estimated mass"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(148, 163, 184); margin-top: 2px;"},"16100 kg"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"What the bare structure weighs. A bridge must carry itself before it carries anything else."]],["DIV",{"style":"padding: 8px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--allo-stem-canvas, #0f172a); border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155);"},["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px;"},"Estimated material cost"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(134, 239, 172); margin-top: 2px;"},"$96601"],["DIV",{"style":"font-size: 10px; color: var(--allo-stem-text-soft, #94a3b8); margin-top: 3px; line-height: 1.45;"},"The engineering game: the CHEAPEST design that is still SAFE wins."]]],["DETAILS",{"style":"margin-bottom: 12px; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); background: var(--allo-stem-panel, #1e293b); padding: 10px 14px;"},["SUMMARY",{"style":"font-size: 13px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #e2e8f0); cursor: pointer;"},"📖 The words on this page, in plain language"],["DL",{"style":"margin: 10px 0px 0px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #cbd5e1); line-height: 1.6; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 8px 18px;"},["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Tension — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"A pulling force, like a tug-of-war rope. Shown in red."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Compression — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"A squeezing force, like pressing on a soda can. Shown in blue."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Truss — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"A frame of triangles. Triangles cannot change shape without changing a side length, which makes them stiff."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Member / chord / diagonal — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Any single piece is a member. The long top and bottom pieces are chords; the zig-zags are diagonals."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Yield — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"The point where a material stops springing back and permanently bends or tears. Passing it is a strength failure."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Buckling — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"When a long thin piece under squeeze suddenly snaps sideways, far below its crushing strength. Press a spaghetti noodle from both ends to feel it."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Safety factor — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Calculated capacity divided by the current demand. At 1.0 the model reaches a limit. This lab uses 2.0 as a learning target; real design uses code-specific load and resistance factors."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Governing — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Engineer-speak for \"the one that decides\". The governing member is the weakest link; the governing check is whichever fails first."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"kN (kilonewton) — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"A unit of force. 1 kN is roughly the weight of a washing machine; a car weighs about 15 kN."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"MPa (megapascal) — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Pressure: force concentrated on an area. The same push hurts more through a thumbtack than a book cover; that is higher MPa."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Span — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"The open distance the bridge must cross without support underneath."]],["DIV",{},["DT",{"style":"font-weight: 800; color: rgb(251, 191, 36); display: inline;"},"Slenderness — "],["DD",{"style":"display: inline; margin: 0px;"},"Length compared to thickness. A pencil is stubby; an uncooked spaghetti noodle is slender. Slender pieces buckle easily."]]]],["SECTION",{"style":"padding: 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--allo-stem-panel, #1e293b); border-top: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); border-right: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); border-left: 3px solid rgb(125, 211, 252); margin-bottom: 12px;"},["H3",{"style":"margin-top: 0px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 800; color: var(--allo-stem-text, #e2e8f0); margin-bottom: 8px;"},"Test the whole crossing"],["DIV",{"data-bridge-sweep":"true"},["P",{"style":"font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0px 0px 10px;"},"A passing result at one position can hide a weaker position elsewhere. Test the vehicle at every load-transfer joint and at 2% intervals across the span."],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","style":"padding: 9px 12px; min-height: 40px; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid rgb(100, 116, 139); background: rgb(15, 23, 42); color: rgb(226, 232, 240); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer;"},"Test all positions"]]],["SECTION",{"style":"padding: 14px; border-radius: 12px; background: var(--allo-stem-panel, #1e293b); border-top: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); border-right: 1px solid var(--allo-stem-border, #334155); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--allo-stem